cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite the specific version; these are exploratory, AI-adjudicated pilot results."
type: dataset
title: "Can newer models detect scientific errors? A text-only reviewer pilot with GPT-6-Luna and GPT-6.1-Sol"
authors:
  - family-names: Dackam
    given-names: Richardson
    affiliation: "Nshipyard; independent researcher"
    website: "https://richackam.com"
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-10-01
url: "https://richardsondx.github.io/llm-peer-review-evidence/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/richardsondx/llm-peer-review-evidence"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: "Exploratory evaluation of GPT-6-Luna and GPT-6.1-Sol as manuscript reviewers on 27 identical text-only SPOT inputs. Each model produces one fresh review per manuscript; paired, identity-blinded automated adjudication measures matching to published annotations. A 12-annotation specificity screen defines primary coverage. No independent human validation, negative controls, human reviewer comparison, confidence calibration or general reliability claim. The original 27-study literature audit is archived separately."
keywords:
  - scientific peer review
  - large language models
  - scientific error detection
  - exploratory evaluation
